# Track application questionnaire -> "APEX Track Applications" Notion database (must live in the APEX OS workspace)
# 1. Create the database in APEX OS with these exact columns (names are case-sensitive):
#      Name (Title), Email (Email), LinkedIn Profile (URL), Military Track (Text),
#      Track Interested (Select: Architects, Founders), Why (Text),
#      Status (Select: New, Reviewed, Accepted), Submitted (Created time, optional)
# 2. In the APEX OS workspace, create an internal integration (Settings -> Connections -> integrations,
#    or notion.so/my-integrations with APEX OS selected) and copy its secret (starts with "ntn_").
# 3. Open the database -> ... menu -> Connections -> connect your integration.
# 4. Set the two values below in .env.local, and in the Vercel project settings for production.
NOTION_TOKEN=
NOTION_APPLICATIONS_DB_ID=
